{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3058","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3058","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3058\",\"parent_revision\":\"e41135df84f207ec5483583b1c16144fa4acc0a1\",\"root_revision\":\"6c082d43c12da2a5c134c1693a20df7e41baa6c180ea6b3a7e3003083d208713\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nPlan reads, task reads, and artifact content reads return whole documents with no size guard. Harnesses commonly cap a single tool response near 10,000 tokens. Artifacts can be full architecture specifications or codebase analyses; a ready-task listing returns every task body at once.\\n\\nExisting plan and task documentation is silent on content size \u2014 it does not acknowledge that large plans or tasks exist.\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-09-20T10:08:28.927871Z</sub>\\n\\nRT-ICA Snapshot: refactor: route plan, task, and artifact reads through the markdown engine\\nDate: 2026-09-20\\nGoal: Every plan read, task read, artifact content read, and ready-task listing returns a usable response within the token budget, with the whole of a large document reachable across successive calls.\\nConditions:\\n1. The affected read surfaces are identified with their locations | Status: AVAILABLE\\n2. Whether any of the four surfaces applies a token budget today | Status: AVAILABLE\\n3. The budget constant to apply, and how it resolves | Status: AVAILABLE\\n4. The normative behaviour required of an over-budget response | Status: AVAILABLE\\n5. Whether any prior implementation of this issue exists | Status: AVAILABLE\\n6. Output-schema headroom available for new response fields | Status: AVAILABLE\\n7. Which existing callers consume the four surfaces and would see a changed response shape | Status: DERIVABLE\\n8. What the plan and task documentation currently says about content size | Status: DERIVABLE\\n9. Whether the engine's navigator can address a structured plan or task record, or only free markdown | Status: DERIVABLE\\n10. Whether a ready-task listing's size is bounded by task count, document size, or both | Status: DERIVABLE\\n11. The scope boundary between this issue and #3078 for artifact content reads | Status: MISSING\\nAVAILABLE count: 6\\nDERIVABLE count: 4\\nMISSING count: 1\\nDecision: APPROVED-WITH-GAPS\\n\\nNotes on the conditions, with evidence, verified on 7e6381259:\\n\\n1. Four surfaces: sam_plan (sam_schema/server.py:95), sam_task (sam_schema/server.py:167), artifact_read (backlog_core/server.py:3522), backlog_get_ready_sam_tasks (backlog_core/server.py:3606).\\n2. None. sam_schema/server.py contains no token-budget constant. backlog_view and backlog_list apply their own; these four do not.\\n3. _DEFAULT_BUDGET at progressive_markdown/models.py:15, resolving to MAX_MCP_OUTPUT_TOKENS - 500, falling back to 9,500. R2 requires the budget to come from one constant.\\n4. docs/agent-markdown-consumption-contract.md. R2 forbids dropping, eliding or truncating any addressable node to fit a budget. R3 requires the compact form to be returned automatically, with no caller opt-in.\\n5. No prior implementation. PR #3551's description lists #3058 among the issues still tracking this work.\\n6. backlog_view's own schema measures 1,706 tokens against a 2,000 ceiling. The total across all tools measures 12,773 against the 13,000 ceiling in tests/test_tool_output_schemas.py, leaving 227 tokens. The total is the binding constraint.\\n11. This is the one condition a tool cannot settle. #3058 covers \\\"artifact content reads\\\". #3078 is titled \\\"artifact content delivery bypasses the markdown engine entirely\\\" and states that artifact_read() returns raw content with no parsing, navigation or pagination. Both appear to own the same surface. Either #3078 is a subset of this issue, or one of the two drops artifact reads from its scope. Two plans touching artifact_read would collide the way #3057 and #3059 do on disclosure_handler.py. The owner decides.\\n\\nThis is the pre-swarm baseline. The rtica-assessor's final pass in finalize.md supersedes it.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Issue Classification\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-09-20T10:20:50.452248Z</sub>\\n\\n**Type**: recurring-pattern\\n\\n**Rationale**: Walking the decision tree: Q1 (procedural?) = NO \u2014 this requires design work and coordination across five surfaces. Q2 (same problem class 2+ times?) = YES \u2014 verified three independent token-budget implementations exist: (1) `backlog_core/server.py:231` defines `_VIEW_TOKEN_BUDGET = 4_000` for `backlog_view`, using its own pagination logic; (2) `backlog_core/server.py:1659` implements `_resolve_effective_limit` for `backlog_list`, applying its own token-budget path; (3) `sam_schema/server_plan_ops.py:54` defines a comment `# Token budget for auto-pagination: 4400 tokens` and `sam_schema/server_plan_ops.py:131` implements `_paginate_results`, applying its own token-budget logic with binary search. None of these three imports `progressive_markdown` for pagination (verified by grep of imports at head of each file). The common violation: each implements token-budget pagination independently, violating the design requirement that \\\"no response from the five surfaces exceeds the configured token budget.\\\" **Analysis Method**: 6-sigma frequency analysis via backlog history search.\\n\\n**Scenario Target**: Current state \u2014 developers build new read surfaces or extend existing ones without architectural mandate to use shared engine, leading to unbounded responses that exceed harness caps. Desired state \u2014 all token-budget pagination (existing and future) routes through `progressive_markdown` under one enforced constant, with no reimplementation.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Plan read, task read, and artifact content read route through the markdown engine\\n- [ ] Each returns the compact form automatically when over budget, per R3\\n- [ ] A listing operation does not embed unbounded bodies\\n- [ ] No response can exceed the configured budget regardless of stored document size\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Priority**: P0 \u2014 unbounded responses against a hard harness cap fail rather than degrade\\n- Intended behaviour is defined in `plugins/development-harness/docs/agent-markdown-consumption-contract.md`. Component ownership is defined in `plugins/development-harness/docs/component-architecture.md`. Parent: #3054.\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"ea50704fd4063e42b3bbe4c165587f2ec08b37748b164d721c065d2d898b0751\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABVq3T6Q\"}"}